    "DutyRequest": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "POST /driver/v1/duty",
      "properties": {
        "changeId": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "expectedEndAt": {
          "description": "⚠ OPTIONAL, AND ITS ABSENCE MEANS UNKNOWN (061, FR-032/FR-033).\n\nWhen a driver goes on duty they may say when they expect to finish. It buys nothing today — it exists so the dispatch slice can ask \"can this driver finish this round before they go home\", which is otherwise unanswerable.\n\n⚠ IT MUST NEVER BE DEFAULTED TO A SHIFT LENGTH. An invented finish time would make a guess look like a fact at exactly the moment it decides someone's workload — and the driver would be the one who found out.",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "onDuty": {
          "type": "boolean"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "onDuty",
        "changeId"
      ],
